---
/**
 * Track 8 (Visual Math: Calculus), Lesson 3, illustration 1 of 2.
 *
 * The geometric power rule for t². A square of side t (with t = 4 for the
 * picture) is grown by dt = 0.6 on the top and right edges. Two thin
 * strips are added, each of area t·dt, plus a small dt-by-dt corner block.
 * Total added area = 2t·dt + dt². As dt shrinks, the dt² term vanishes
 * relative to the 2t·dt term, leaving d(t²)/dt = 2t.
 */

const cx = 80; // svg origin x for the square's lower-left
const cy = 290; // svg origin y for the square's lower-left
const SCALE = 50; // pixels per unit

const t = 4;
const dt = 0.6;

const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';
const PINK = '#be185d';
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca-sqstrips-title ca-sqstrips-desc">
		<title id="ca-sqstrips-title">A square of side t grown by dt: added area equals 2t dt plus dt squared</title>
		<desc id="ca-sqstrips-desc">A square of side t equals 4 is drawn at the lower-left, filled in light teal, with area labeled t squared. Two thin strips of width dt equals 0.6 are added along the top edge (4 wide by 0.6 tall, filled amber) and the right edge (0.6 wide by 4 tall, filled amber), each labeled t times dt. A small purple square in the upper-right corner has size dt by dt and is labeled dt squared. The total added area is therefore 2 times t dt plus dt squared. A note below summarizes that as dt shrinks, the corner dt squared becomes negligible, giving the derivative of t squared as 2t.</desc>

		{/* original square t×t */}
		<rect x={cx} y={cy - t * SCALE} width={t * SCALE} height={t * SCALE} fill={TEAL} fill-opacity="0.18" stroke={TEAL} stroke-width="1.6" />

		{/* top strip: t wide × dt tall, sitting on top of the square */}
		<rect x={cx} y={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE} width={t * SCALE} height={dt * SCALE} fill={AMBER} fill-opacity="0.4" stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.3" />

		{/* right strip: dt wide × t tall */}
		<rect x={cx + t * SCALE} y={cy - t * SCALE} width={dt * SCALE} height={t * SCALE} fill={AMBER} fill-opacity="0.4" stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.3" />

		{/* corner dt×dt block */}
		<rect x={cx + t * SCALE} y={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE} width={dt * SCALE} height={dt * SCALE} fill={PINK} fill-opacity="0.5" stroke={PINK} stroke-width="1.3" />

		{/* labels */}
		{/* original square label */}
		<text x={cx + (t * SCALE) / 2} y={cy - (t * SCALE) / 2 + 6} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="20" font-weight="700" fill={TEAL}>t²</text>

		{/* top strip label */}
		<text x={cx + (t * SCALE) / 2} y={cy - (t + dt / 2) * SCALE + 5} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>t · dt</text>

		{/* right strip label */}
		<text x={cx + (t + dt / 2) * SCALE} y={cy - (t * SCALE) / 2} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER} transform={`rotate(-90 ${cx + (t + dt / 2) * SCALE} ${cy - (t * SCALE) / 2})`}>t · dt</text>

		{/* corner label */}
		<text x={cx + (t + dt / 2) * SCALE + 22} y={cy - (t + dt / 2) * SCALE + 4} font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill={PINK}>dt²</text>
		<line x1={cx + (t + dt / 2) * SCALE + 18} y1={cy - (t + dt / 2) * SCALE} x2={cx + (t + dt) * SCALE + 2} y2={cy - (t + dt / 2) * SCALE} stroke={PINK} stroke-width="1" opacity="0.65" />

		{/* dimension brackets along the bottom (showing t) and right (showing t) */}
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy + 14} x2={cx + t * SCALE} y2={cy + 14} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6" />
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy + 10} x2={cx} y2={cy + 18} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6" />
		<line x1={cx + t * SCALE} y1={cy + 10} x2={cx + t * SCALE} y2={cy + 18} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6" />
		<text x={cx + (t * SCALE) / 2} y={cy + 30} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">t</text>

		{/* dt bracket along top */}
		<line x1={cx + t * SCALE + 4} y1={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 14} x2={cx + (t + dt) * SCALE + 4} y2={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 14} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6" />
		<line x1={cx + t * SCALE + 4} y1={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 10} x2={cx + t * SCALE + 4} y2={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 18} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6" />
		<line x1={cx + (t + dt) * SCALE + 4} y1={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 10} x2={cx + (t + dt) * SCALE + 4} y2={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 18} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6" />
		<text x={cx + (t + dt / 2) * SCALE + 4} y={cy - (t + dt) * SCALE - 22} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">dt</text>

		{/* legend with the algebra */}
		<g transform="translate(420, 100)">
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="290" height="170" rx="6" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.04" />
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="290" height="170" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.3" />
			<text x="145" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">added area when t grows by dt:</text>
			<text x="145" y="54" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" fill="currentColor">
				<tspan fill={AMBER} font-weight="700">2 · (t · dt)</tspan> + <tspan fill={PINK} font-weight="700">dt²</tspan>
			</text>
			<text x="145" y="82" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">two strips + one corner</text>
			<text x="145" y="112" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">as dt → 0, dt² vanishes faster</text>
			<text x="145" y="138" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>
				d(t²) / dt = 2t
			</text>
			<text x="145" y="158" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.55">the power rule, seen geometrically</text>
		</g>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>Grow a square of side t by a small dt. You add two thin strips (one on top, one on the right), each of area t times dt, plus a tiny dt-by-dt corner square. As dt shrinks, the corner shrinks faster than the strips do, so it vanishes from the rate. The derivative of t² is 2t, two strips' worth of growth per unit of new side.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 740px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
